The shared frontend developer SDK for the Thebes Layer 1 example applications:
a browser boundary client, a Memphis passkey authentication client, a typed
query/update layer, and React hooks. It is implemented in TypeScript with one
third-party runtime file: runtime/noble-ed25519-3.1.0.js, the unmodified
index.js of @noble/ed25519 3.1.0 (MIT License, (c) 2019 Paul Miller,
https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-ed25519; npm integrity verified at
download; SHA-256 fe893bfb9286c67892a45c18537035eab3325bc723bb2855ddcb9e9cb57df9aa).
passkey.js loads it only in a browser without WebCrypto Ed25519, to sign
updates.

The Motoko backend library is distributed separately as thebes-lib
(https://github.com/Mercatura-Forum/thebes-lib).

The contracts are written in Motoko and speak Candid, both developed by the
DFINITY Foundation (https://dfinity.org). With thanks to the DFINITY team for
their excellent work.

